From 88890765115d7599fce36f0de26b8d4a38bb3e02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 16:18:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] fix(plugin): stop telling agents to run bd init on
 database errors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The troubleshooting table told agents to run `bd init <prefix>` when
they hit "database not found". Without --server flag, this overwrites
metadata.json dolt_mode to "embedded", breaking all server-mode repos.

This was the root cause of repeated server-mode breakage across
projects — agents would hit a transient error, follow the SKILL.md
advice, and silently switch the entire project to embedded mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/beads/skills/beads/SKILL.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugins/beads/skills/beads/SKILL.md b/plugins/beads/skills/beads/SKILL.md
index 5a1968523..def3984b5 100644
--- a/plugins/beads/skills/beads/SKILL.md
+++ b/plugins/beads/skills/beads/SKILL.md
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ Append `--json` to any command for structured output. Use `bd show <id> --long`
 
 | Error | Fix |
 |-------|-----|
-| `database not found` | `bd init <prefix>` in project root |
+| `database not found` | Check `.beads/metadata.json` exists and `dolt_mode` matches `config.yaml`. Do NOT run `bd init` — it overwrites server config. |
 | `not in a git repository` | `git init` first |
 | `disk I/O error (522)` | Move `.beads/` off cloud-synced filesystem |
 | Status updates lag | Use server mode: `bd dolt start` |
